  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "POINTER\n\nThe pointer nest holds one\nthing: [across | away], in\nthe table's own steps.\n\nA position is a reading, not\na history, so each new one\nreplaces the last instead of\npiling up.\n\nThe Watcher keeps the\ncurrent one in a hole where\nyou can see it."
   },
   "x": -1.45,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "TO RUN IT\n\nSet Rounds to 2000 and give\nthe work box to the Watcher.\n\nNow move the pointer over the\ntable. The two numbers in the\nsecond hole follow it.\n\nIts three steps are: sweep\nthe old reading away, take\nwhat is on the nest, put it\nin the hole. Nothing about\nthe pointer is built in -- it\nis a box arriving as mail."
   },
   "x": -0.75,
   "z": 2.15
  },
  {
   "thing": {
    "kind": "text",
    "text": "WHAT IT IS FOR\n\nAnything that reads a number\ncan read this one: a scale\ncan weigh it, a robot can\ncompare it, a bird can carry\nit into a house.\n\nZero across is the middle of\nthe table; away grows towards\nyou. So the numbers are worth\nwatching as you move -- they\nare the table's own\ncoordinates, not the screen's."
   },
   "x": -0.05,
   "z": 2.15
  }
